{#
  Confirm dialog wrapper (2.6, theme partial `confirm_dialog`): a Stimulus `confirm-dialog` root (stimulus-peers/
  confirm_dialog_controller.ts: open / close, type-to-confirm, body portal, open on connect), an optional trigger
  button and a native <dialog> whose body is the `form` block — the apps' shared/_confirm_dialog.html.twig, same
  options and blocks. Embed it:

      {% embed nowo_ui_partial('confirm_dialog') with {trigger_label: 'Revoke', dialog_modifier: 'nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--lg'} %}
          {% block form %}{{ form_start(form) }}…<button type="button" data-confirm-dialog-close>Cancel</button>{{ form_end(form) }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}

  Modes:
    - full (default): wrapper (data-controller="confirm-dialog") + trigger + dialog
    - only_dialog: true — the dialog only (controller and trigger live in the parent template); wrapper: false — the
      same, kept for the apps' copies

  Options:
    - trigger_label (the default trigger renders only with it), trigger_class (default the `confirm_dialog_trigger`
      slot), trigger_title, trigger_aria_label, trigger_testid, trigger_disabled
    - expected_value: type-to-confirm value (data-confirm-dialog-expected-value; the input is the confirmInput target)
    - open_on_connect: true opens the dialog when the controller connects (only an explicit true / 1 / 'true')
    - dialog_id: id of the <dialog> (e.g. the `?new=1` target of partials/_open_modal_on_load.html.twig). With an id the
      dialog also works without Stimulus through js/nowo-ui-confirm.js: the trigger gets data-nowo-confirm-open /
      data-nowo-confirm-target and [data-nowo-confirm-close] closes it
    - dialog_testid, aria_labelledby
    - dialog_modifier: extra classes on the <dialog> (e.g. confirm-dialog--xl), after the `confirm_dialog` slot;
      `nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--plain` drops the kit box (background, border, shadow, padding, size) — 2.6.1
    - attr / dialog_attr: extra attributes of the wrapper / the dialog (no on*)
    - bundle: per-bundle theme exceptions
  Anatomy (2.29, opt-in with `anatomy: true`): the dialog renders the kit dialog sections instead of the free `form`
  panel — header (title, optional status badge, close ×), body (the `body` block, the only part that scrolls) and
  footer (the `footer` block, outside the body, always visible: Cancel / Close then the one primary, on the right). A
  form in the body is bound to its submit in the footer with the `form` attribute:

      {% embed nowo_ui_partial('confirm_dialog') with {anatomy: true, trigger_label: 'Edit', title: 'Edit monitor', dialog_id: 'edit-monitor'} %}
          {% block body %}{{ form_start(form, {attr: {id: 'edit-monitor-form'}}) }}…{{ form_end(form) }}{% endblock %}
          {% block footer %}
              <button type="button" class="{{ nowo_ui_class('btn_secondary') }}" data-confirm-dialog-close>Cancel</button>
              <button type="submit" form="edit-monitor-form" class="{{ nowo_ui_class('btn_primary') }}">Save</button>
          {% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}

  Only with `anatomy: true` (an explicit true; any other value, missing or inherited from the context, keeps the
  2.28 markup byte for byte, whatever `title`, `status` or `size` the context holds):
    - title (string or View\Label) / title_html (trusted HTML printed raw — escape what you interpolate)
    - status: View\PageStatus or a hash {label, tone (success | danger | warning | neutral | info; any other tone →
      neutral), title, attributes}; any other value is ignored (no badge) — View\PageStatus::fromOption()
    - size: md (default) | wide → the two dialog sizes (docs/PAGE_CONTRACT.md "Dialog sizes and anatomy"). A free
      panel takes the sizes from its modifier: nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--sm → medium, --lg / --xl → wide. With a
      field, list, table or fold the height is the content's, capped at the size's (2.31; theme.dialog.height: size =
      the size's height); a plain yes / no keeps its natural height
    - close_label (default action.close), dismissible (default true: the × button)
    - title_id (default <dialog_id>-title, else a generated id): the id of the header <h2>; the dialog's
      aria-labelledby points to it unless aria_labelledby is given. The anatomy always renders that <h2>; the `form`
      block is not rendered (the `body` block's default is the `form` block, so an existing form panel moves into the
      body as is)
  Phone sheet, header steps and body sections (2.63, anatomy only, every option optional; the 2.62 markup and layout are
  unchanged without them):
    - phone: 'inset' (default) | 'sheet'. 'sheet' makes the dialog fill the screen at 40rem and below (the
      `nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--sheet` class): header and footer stay, only the body scrolls, the safe areas
      (notch, home indicator) are kept, and the native modal dialog still traps focus, closes on Escape and gives focus
      back to the opener. Any other value is the default. Wide dialogs and dialogs with many fields or steps should take it
    - header_steps: list of the `steps` partial's items ({label, status, hint, href}); header_steps_label: accessible
      name of the list. Rendered inside the header (it stays when the body scrolls), compact on phones (only the
      current step shows its label). The `header_steps` block replaces it with any markup
    - Dividers between body sections: put `<section class="nowo-ui-section">` blocks (class slot `section`, without
      `nowo-ui-card`) in the body; each one after the first gets a divider and the form row gap above it
  On demand (2.68, `dialog_src`): the page renders only the opener and an empty dialog shell; the body is fetched when the
  dialog opens (the `remote_form_dialog` partial and js/nowo-ui-dialog.js: `X-Nowo-Dialog: 1`, 422 re-rendered in place,
  204 + X-Nowo-Redirect followed, Nowo\UiKitBundle\Dialog\RemoteDialogResponder on the server). Hosts must not render a
  dialog's form before it is opened: a hidden edit form per row costs the whole form tree on every page view.

      {% embed nowo_ui_partial('confirm_dialog') with {dialog_src: path('member_edit', {id: m.id}), dialog_id: 'edit-member-' ~ m.id, trigger_label: 'Edit', title: 'Edit member', size: 'wide'} %}{% endembed %}

    - dialog_src: URL of the dialog's own page (the full page without JavaScript, its fragment for X-Nowo-Dialog: 1).
      Only a non-empty string turns the mode on: anything else (missing, null, '', false, a number, an object) keeps
      the inline markup above byte for byte. A javascript:, vbscript:, data: or blob: URL keeps the mode (no body)
      but prints a disabled opener and no opener attributes (SafeHref, as the `back_link` and `tree` partials).
      The `form`, `body`, `footer` and `header_steps` blocks are not rendered; `anatomy`, `phone`, `expected_value`,
      `open_on_connect`, `status` and the Stimulus `confirm-dialog` root do not apply (the fragment carries its own
      heading, actions and type-to-confirm). The default trigger is a link `<a href="<dialog_src>">` (a disabled
      `<button>` with trigger_disabled); a custom `trigger` block prints `dialog_opener_attr` with
      nowo_ui_html_attrs() on its own `<a href="{{ dialog_opener_href }}">` (null for a script URL)
    - dialog_id (default a generated id), title (the dialog title, else the opener's text), size (md default | wide;
      dialog_modifier --lg / --xl → wide), placement, labels, follow_on_load_error, backdrop_close, dialog_testid, dialog_attr: passed to the
      shell (`remote_form_dialog`)
    - dialog_shell: false renders only the opener; give it a dialog_id (a generated id matches no shell). Many rows
      share one shell rendered once with only_dialog: true, dialog_shell: true and the same dialog_id (no dialog_src
      needed: each opener loads its own); only_dialog: true with a dialog_src renders only the shell too
  Blocks: trigger (the default button), header_steps (2.63), form (the free dialog content: a Symfony form_start / form_end or any panel),
  body / footer (2.29, the anatomy sections, only with anatomy: true).
  Close: [data-confirm-dialog-close] (Stimulus) or [data-nowo-confirm-close] (kit runtime), Escape.
  Slots: confirm_dialog_root, confirm_dialog, confirm_dialog_trigger.
#}
{% set bundle = bundle|default(null) %}
{% set _only_dialog = only_dialog|default(false) or not (wrapper ?? true) %}
{% set _dialog_id = dialog_id|default(null) %}
{% set _open_on_connect = open_on_connect|default(false) in [true, 1, '1', 'true', 'TRUE'] %}
{% set _expected = expected_value ?? null %}
{% set _anatomy = (anatomy ?? false) is same as(true) %}
{% set _sheet = _anatomy and (phone ?? 'inset') is same as('sheet') %}
{% set _dialog_class = (nowo_ui_class('confirm_dialog', bundle) ~ (_anatomy and size|default('md') == 'wide' ? ' nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--wide') ~ (_sheet ? ' nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--sheet') ~ (_anatomy ? ' nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--anatomy') ~ ' ' ~ dialog_modifier|default(''))|trim %}
{% set _title_id = _anatomy ? (title_id|default(null) ?: ((_dialog_id ?? ('nowo-ui-confirm-dialog-' ~ random(100000, 999999))) ~ '-title')) : null %}
{% set _labelledby = (aria_labelledby is defined and aria_labelledby) ? aria_labelledby : _title_id %}
{#- 2.68: on demand — only the opener and an empty remote form dialog shell (see "On demand" above) -#}
{#- only a non-empty string (a number, a Stringable or a hash keeps the inline markup) -#}
{% set _src = (dialog_src ?? null) is not empty and dialog_src is not iterable and dialog_src is same as(dialog_src ~ '') ? dialog_src : null %}
{#- a javascript:, vbscript:, data: or blob: URL (SafeHref, as back_link / tree) opens nothing: no link, a disabled opener -#}
{% set _src_url = _src is not null and not nowo_ui_theme.hrefRunsScript(_src) ? _src : null %}
{#- the shared shell of many openers (dialog_shell: false on each): only_dialog + an explicit dialog_shell: true -#}
{% set _shell_only = _only_dialog and (dialog_shell ?? null) is same as(true) %}
{% if _src is not null or _shell_only %}
{% set _src_id = _dialog_id ?: 'nowo-ui-dialog-' ~ random(100000, 999999) %}
{% set _src_title = (title ?? null) is not empty ? title|nowo_ui_trans : null %}
{% set _src_modifier = dialog_modifier|default('') %}
{% set _src_size = (size ?? null) in ['wide', 'lg', 'xl'] or 'nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--lg' in _src_modifier or 'nowo-ui-confirm-dialog--xl' in _src_modifier ? 'lg' : 'md' %}
{% set dialog_opener_href = _src_url %}
{% set dialog_opener_attr = _src_url is null ? {} : nowo_ui_remote_form_opener(_src_id, _src_title, false, _src_url)|merge({'aria-haspopup': 'dialog', 'aria-controls': _src_id}) %}
{% if not _only_dialog %}
<div class="{{ nowo_ui_class('confirm_dialog_root', bundle) }}{{ (attr.class ?? false) ? ' ' ~ attr.class }}" data-nowo-ui-lazy-dialog{{ nowo_ui_attrs('confirm_dialog_root', bundle, nowo_ui_attrs_without_class(attr|default({}))) }}>
    {{ block('trigger') }}
{% endif %}
{% if dialog_shell ?? true %}
{{ include(nowo_ui_partial('remote_form_dialog', bundle), {
    id: _src_id,
    title: _src_title ?? (trigger_label ?? null),
    size: _src_size,
    placement: placement ?? 'center',
    labels: labels ?? {},
    backdrop_close: backdrop_close ?? false,
    follow_on_load_error: follow_on_load_error ?? true,
    attr: (dialog_attr|default({}))|merge(dialog_testid|default(null) ? {'data-testid': dialog_testid} : {}),
    bundle: bundle,
}, false) }}
{% endif %}
{% if not _only_dialog %}
</div>
{% endif %}
{% else %}

{% if not _only_dialog %}
<div class="{{ nowo_ui_class('confirm_dialog_root', bundle) }}{{ (attr.class ?? false) ? ' ' ~ attr.class }}" data-controller="confirm-dialog"{% if _expected is not null %} data-confirm-dialog-expected-value="{{ _expected }}"{% endif %}{% if _open_on_connect %} data-confirm-dialog-open-on-connect-value="true"{% endif %}{{ nowo_ui_attrs('confirm_dialog_root', bundle, nowo_ui_attrs_without_class(attr|default({}))) }}>
    {% block trigger %}
        {% if _src is not null %}
            {% if trigger_label is defined and (trigger_disabled|default(false) or _src_url is null) %}
            <button type="button" class="{{ trigger_class|default(nowo_ui_class('confirm_dialog_trigger', bundle)) }}"{% if trigger_title is defined %} title="{{ trigger_title }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_aria_label is defined %} aria-label="{{ trigger_aria_label }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_testid is defined %} data-testid="{{ trigger_testid }}"{% endif %} disabled{{ nowo_ui_attrs('confirm_dialog_trigger', bundle) }}>{{ trigger_label }}</button>
            {% elseif trigger_label is defined %}
            <a href="{{ _src_url }}" class="{{ trigger_class|default(nowo_ui_class('confirm_dialog_trigger', bundle)) }}"{{ nowo_ui_html_attrs(dialog_opener_attr) }}{% if trigger_title is defined %} title="{{ trigger_title }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_aria_label is defined %} aria-label="{{ trigger_aria_label }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_testid is defined %} data-testid="{{ trigger_testid }}"{% endif %}{{ nowo_ui_attrs('confirm_dialog_trigger', bundle) }}>{{ trigger_label }}</a>
            {% endif %}
        {% elseif trigger_label is defined %}
            <button type="button" class="{{ trigger_class|default(nowo_ui_class('confirm_dialog_trigger', bundle)) }}" data-action="confirm-dialog#open"{% if _dialog_id %} data-nowo-confirm-open data-nowo-confirm-target="{{ _dialog_id }}" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="{{ _dialog_id }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_title is defined %} title="{{ trigger_title }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_aria_label is defined %} aria-label="{{ trigger_aria_label }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_testid is defined %} data-testid="{{ trigger_testid }}"{% endif %}{% if trigger_disabled|default(false) %} disabled{% endif %}{{ nowo_ui_attrs('confirm_dialog_trigger', bundle) }}>{{ trigger_label }}</button>
        {% endif %}
    {% endblock %}
{% endif %}
<dialog class="{{ _dialog_class }}{{ (dialog_attr.class ?? false) ? ' ' ~ dialog_attr.class }}" data-confirm-dialog-target="dialog"{% if _dialog_id %} id="{{ _dialog_id }}" data-nowo-ui-confirm{% endif %}{% if dialog_testid|default(null) %} data-testid="{{ dialog_testid }}"{% endif %}{% if _labelledby %} aria-labelledby="{{ _labelledby }}"{% endif %}{{ nowo_ui_attrs('confirm_dialog', bundle, nowo_ui_attrs_without_class(dialog_attr|default({}))) }}>
{% if _anatomy %}
    {% set _status = nowo_ui_dialog_status(status ?? null) %}
    {% set _close_label = close_label|default('action.close'|trans({}, 'NowoUiKitBundle')) %}
    <header class="{{ nowo_ui_class('dialog_header', bundle) }}"{{ nowo_ui_attrs('dialog_header', bundle) }}>
        {% if _status %}<div class="nowo-ui-dialog__title-row">{% endif %}<h2 class="{{ nowo_ui_class('dialog_title', bundle) }}" id="{{ _title_id }}"{{ nowo_ui_attrs('dialog_title', bundle) }}>{% if title_html|default(null) %}{{ title_html|raw }}{% else %}{{ title|default(null)|nowo_ui_trans }}{% endif %}</h2>{% if _status %}{{ include(nowo_ui_partial('page_status', bundle), {status: _status, bundle: bundle}, false)|trim|raw }}</div>{% endif %}

        {% if dismissible ?? true %}
            <button type="button" class="nowo-ui-dialog__close" data-confirm-dialog-close{% if _dialog_id %} data-nowo-confirm-close{% endif %} aria-label="{{ _close_label }}" title="{{ _close_label }}"><span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span></button>
        {% endif -%}
        {%- set _header_steps %}{% block header_steps %}{% if (header_steps ?? null) is iterable and header_steps is not empty %}{{ include(nowo_ui_partial('steps', bundle), {items: header_steps, label: header_steps_label ?? null, attr: {class: 'nowo-ui-steps--compact'}}, false) }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}{% endset -%}
        {%- if _header_steps|trim is not empty %}
        <div class="nowo-ui-dialog__steps">{{ _header_steps|trim|raw }}</div>
        {% endif %}
    </header>
    <div class="{{ nowo_ui_class('dialog_body', bundle) }}"{{ nowo_ui_attrs('dialog_body', bundle) }}>
        {%- block body %}{{ block('form') }}{% endblock -%}
    </div>
    <footer class="{{ nowo_ui_class('dialog_footer', bundle) }}"{{ nowo_ui_attrs('dialog_footer', bundle) }}>
        {%- block footer %}{% endblock -%}
    </footer>
{% else %}
    {% block form %}{% endblock %}
{% endif %}
</dialog>
{% if not _only_dialog %}
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
